{"id": "20523839", "revid": "27823944", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20523839", "title": "Larkin's Hundred", "text": "Larkin's Hundred, also known as The Castle, is a historic home at Harwood, Anne Arundel County, Maryland, United States. It is a two-story brick house. Although tradition holds that it was built in 1704 by Thomas Larkin, a son of John Larkin of nearby Larkin's Hill Farm, evidence suggest it was actually constructed in the second quarter of the 18th century for Captain Joseph Cowman, a mariner and wealthy Quaker. A white clapboard kitchen wing at the west end was added in 1870. A noteworthy interior feature is a graceful stairway of American walnut.\nLarkin's Hundred was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1969."}
