{"id": "20524797", "revid": "4255301", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20524797", "title": "Forward shipwreck site", "text": "The shipwreck site of the motor launch \"Forward\" is located in Lake George, New York approximately three and one half miles north of the village of Lake George. The motor launch was built in 1906 by Gas Engine &amp; Power Co. and Charles L. Seabury &amp; Co., Consolidated (Morris Heights, New York City, New York). It was one of the first gasoline-powered vessels on Lake George. The original owner was William K. Bixby.\nIt is the 21st property listed as a featured property of the week in a program of the National Park Service that began in July, 2008."}
